course: dictionary
lesson: 15011
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Mum handed in her resignation on Monday, so she will leave her job at the end of the month.» Handing in something and leaving at the end of the month tells you resignation means leaving a job by choice.
explain: The same word can also mean the letter that says you are leaving. «Dad wrote a letter of resignation and gave it to his boss.» Here the resignation is a piece of writing, not a feeling.
explain: Resignation can also be a feeling. «Tom looked at the rain with resignation and put his coat back on.» He has accepted that the rain cannot be changed. Look for clues such as looked, sighed or shrugged: they show a feeling, not a job.
fact: A resignation is when you officially leave a job by choice.
fact: A resignation can also be the letter or announcement that says you are leaving a job.
fact: «Resignation» can mean calmly accepting something bad that you cannot change.
fact: Useful phrases: «hand in your resignation», «letter of resignation», «with resignation».
fact: Say it as rez-ig-NAY-shun.
exercise: «The manager's resignation shocked everyone at the office on Friday.» What does resignation mean here? | A new office party | A loud argument | *Leaving a job by choice | A holiday from work
exercise: Mia's teacher says, «Please read Mr Gray's letter of resignation to the class.» What is the letter? | A letter from the hospital | *The letter saying he is leaving his job | A list of school rules | A thank-you card for the class
exercise: «Tom looked at the rain with resignation and put his coat back on.» What does resignation show? | He is going to sing in the rain | *He has accepted that he cannot change the rain | He is very excited about the rain | He is angry with his coat
test: «Grandma said with resignation, "The bus is late again."» What does resignation mean here? | Joy at the bus arriving | *Calm acceptance of something she cannot change | Shouting at the bus driver | Leaving the bus stop
test: Ben hands in his resignation to the shop owner. What has Ben done? | He has lost his bag | *He has officially left his job by choice | He has been given a pay rise | He has broken a shop window
exam: «The company asked for the director's resignation, and she gave it with quiet resignation.» Which two meanings does the word have here? | *Leaving a job, and calmly accepting it | Shouting and whispering | Happy and sad | Winning and losing
